fix(fumadocs): reconcile layout & page integration points with v16 APIs

Per issue #16: fumadocs-core/fumadocs-ui v16's API surface moved out from
under the root layout, docs layout, and source loader, which the prior
dependency-bump ticket (#15) deliberately left broken.

- RootProvider now ships from `fumadocs-ui/provider/next` (framework-scoped
  providers), not the old bare `fumadocs-ui/provider`; the static search
  config shape is unchanged.
- The docs layout's sidebar tab icon transform moved from
  `sidebar.tabs.transform` (now deprecated) to top-level
  `DocsLayoutProps.tabs.transform`. `source.getNodeMeta(node)`'s return type
  dropped `.file.dirname` in favour of a virtualized `.path`; ported the
  per-section color derivation to `PathUtils.dirname(meta.path)` from
  `fumadocs-core/source`, which is the same value under the new API.
- `tsconfig.json`'s `@/.source` path alias now points at `.source/server.ts`
  instead of the no-longer-generated `.source/index.ts` (fumadocs-mdx v15
  splits codegen into server/dynamic/browser files); `server.ts` exposes the
  same `docs` collection with `toFumadocsSource()` that `index.ts` used to,
  so `src/lib/source.ts` needed no changes itself. Also flipped
  `jsx: preserve` -> `react-jsx` (React 19.2's JSX namespace requires it)
  and added `.next/dev/types` to `include`, both auto-applied by `next dev`
  itself on first run.
- `layout.config.tsx`, the home layout, and the catch-all docs page already
  matched the v16 API shapes as written and needed no changes.

Two dependency bumps, within existing package.json semver ranges, were
needed to make `pnpm dev` actually render (not just typecheck), per this
issue's acceptance criteria:
- tailwindcss/@tailwindcss/postcss 4.0.6 -> 4.3.3: fumadocs-ui v16's shipped
  CSS uses the `@source inline(...)` directive, unsupported by the
  0.6-vintage Tailwind that was still resolved in the lockfile.
- @types/react(-dom) 19.0.x -> 19.2.x: React 19.2 ships `useEffectEvent`
  natively (fumadocs-core v16 dropped its `utils/use-effect-event` polyfill
  accordingly), but the stale 19.0 type declarations only had it under
  `experimental_useEffectEvent`.

`src/components/tabs.tsx` imported the removed
