Issue #16 is fully implemented, verified, and committed.

**Summary of what changed:**
- `src/app/layout.tsx` — `RootProvider` import moved from `fumadocs-ui/provider` to `fumadocs-ui/provider/next` (v16 splits providers by framework).
- `src/app/docs/layout.tsx` — sidebar tab `transform` moved from deprecated `sidebar.tabs.transform` to top-level `DocsLayoutProps.tabs.transform`; `meta.file.dirname` (removed from v16's `Meta` type) replaced with `PathUtils.dirname(meta.path)` from `fumadocs-core/source`, preserving identical per-section color derivation.
- `tsconfig.json` — `@/.source` alias repointed at `.source/server.ts` (fumadocs-mdx v15 splits codegen into server/dynamic/browser files instead of one `index.ts`); `jsx: preserve` → `react-jsx` and a `.next/dev/types` include entry, both applied automatically by `next dev` itself.
- `layout.config.tsx`, the home layout, the catch-all docs page, and `src/lib/source.ts` needed no code changes — they already matched v16's shapes.
- `tailwindcss`/`@tailwindcss/postcss` and `@types/react`/`@types/react-dom` bumped within their existing `package.json` ranges — required for `pnpm dev` to actually render (fumadocs-ui v16's CSS uses a newer Tailwind directive; React 19.2's `useEffectEvent` needed newer type declarations).
- `src/components/tabs.tsx` — one-line fix (imported React's native `useEffectEvent` instead of the removed `fumadocs-core/utils/use-effect-event` polyfill, and dropped the now-correctly-recognized stable handle from an effect's dependency array). Not in the issue's file list, but load-bearing: it's pulled in eagerly by `.source/server.ts` via `components.mdx`, so its broken import was 500ing every docs page.

Verified: `tsc --noEmit` and `eslint .` are clean on every touched file (remaining errors are pre-existing, out-of-scope issues in `inline-toc.tsx`, `accordion.tsx`, `banner.tsx`, `use-copy-button.ts` — all flagged as deferred follow-up in the prior ticket's commit). `pnpm dev` renders the home page (logo, nav, Atelier/Xeniapolis menus) and docs pages from both `atelier/` and `xeniapolis/` with correct sidebar tab colors, all as 200s. No MDX content changed. Ran `/code-review`'s two-axis review against the fixed point — both Standards and Spec came back clean (one judgement-call finding, fixed). Work is committed as `c14e96a4`.

